From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/i915, drm/amdgpu: HDMI sinks that drop HPD or reset SCDC
 on a mode change

TVs drop HPD for a moment when they change picture mode: an LG G5 for
about 0.4 s, about 0.4 s after Dolby Vision engages or stops, or after a
refresh rate change. Two things go wrong then.

1. The sink can reset its SCDC TMDS_Config after intel_hdmi_reset_link
read it as matching: it then expects a 1/10 TMDS bit clock ratio while
the source sends 1/40 at 594 MHz, a valid signal the TV shows as "No
signal" until the next modeset (petunia, 2026-10-29: TMDS_Config 0x01
against hdmi_high_tmds_clock_ratio).

i915: after any hotplug of a connected HDMI sink, intel_ddi_hotplug
looks at the sink's SCDC again once a second for 4 s (the
INTEL_HOTPLUG_RETRY path, also when the hotplug changed the connector's
status). intel_hdmi_reset_link does nothing unless the link scrambles or
runs at 1/40, and a modeset only if the sink disagrees; at most 3 such
modesets in 20 s, so a sink that resets again after each one ends with a
wrong link, not an endless blank.

2. Reported as a disconnect, the drop makes the compositor remove the
output and add it back: windows recreated over the video, the saved
configuration applied again (undoing a temporary refresh rate,
resolution and HDR), a blank.

i915: intel_hdmi_detect reports a connected HDMI sink with a CRTC as
still connected (EDID kept) while HPD is low, for up to i915.hpd_hold_ms
(3000; 0 off), and intel_ddi_hotplug looks again every second meanwhile,
so a real unplug is reported when the time is up. Display version 11 and
later (where detect reads the live HPD state).

amdgpu: upstream's HDMI HPD debounce
(amdgpu.hdmi_hpd_debounce_delay_ms, off by default upstream) is on by
default at 3000 ms. A sink that comes back with the same EDID gets no
hotplug event; DC re-enables the stream itself.

Together: no SCDC recheck while HPD is held low. The sink does not
answer then, its TMDS_Config read as 0x00 and intel_hdmi_reset_link made
up to three modesets, 3.5 to 4 s of black after every Dolby Vision stop
on the G5 (petunia, 2026-11-03: 28 drops, 47 "Sink's TMDS config 0x00
doesn't match the link ... modeset", 21 "still wrong after 3 modesets").
HPD coming back is a new hotplug (hotplug_retries from 0), so the 4 s
recheck starts from then, which is when a sink that came back with the
wrong TMDS_Config is fixed.

From big-fella (linux-yblod 7.3-7 and 7.3-8), where kwin-big-fella had
held such an output for 3 s itself (kwin-big-fella-hotplug-hold.patch).

Validation as recorded with the original patches: the HPD hold was "not
yet tested with a sink that drops HPD (the LG B4 on ryzen-fella and the
N150 doesn't); there, boots, forced detects and EDID changes neither
hold nor remove the output".

Regrouped from linux-9913-big-fella-hdmi-scdc-recheck,
linux-9925-big-fella-hdmi-hpd-hold and
linux-9927-big-fella-hdmi-scdc-after-hold (YBLOD 0.3.3 to 0.4.1); no
code change.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_drv.c       | 14 ++++-
 drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_ddi.c      | 62 ++++++++++++++++++-
 .../drm/i915/display/intel_display_types.h    |  9 +++
 drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_hdmi.c     | 56 ++++++++++++++++-
 drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_hotplug.c  |  7 ++-
 5 files changed, 142 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_drv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_drv.c
index d9d794a7db96..dac2f895b5e2 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_drv.c
@@ -245,7 +245,8 @@ int amdgpu_damage_clips = -1; /* auto */
 int amdgpu_umsch_mm_fwlog;
 int amdgpu_rebar = -1; /* auto */
 int amdgpu_user_queue = -1;
-uint amdgpu_hdmi_hpd_debounce_delay_ms;
+/* big-fella: 3000, not 0 (off); see hdmi_hpd_debounce_delay_ms below */
+uint amdgpu_hdmi_hpd_debounce_delay_ms = 3000;
 int amdgpu_ptl = -1; /* auto */
 
 DECLARE_DYNDBG_CLASSMAP(drm_debug_classes, DD_CLASS_TYPE_DISJOINT_BITS, 0,
@@ -1109,8 +1110,15 @@ module_param_named(user_queue, amdgpu_user_queue, int, 0444);
  *
  * Used to filter short disconnect->reconnect HPD toggles some HDMI sinks
  * generate while entering/leaving power save. Set to 0 to disable by default.
- */
-MODULE_PARM_DESC(hdmi_hpd_debounce_delay_ms, "HDMI HPD disconnect debounce delay in milliseconds (0 to disable (by default), 1500 is common)");
+ *
+ * big-fella: 3000 by default. TVs drop HPD for a moment as they change picture
+ * mode (an LG G5 for ~0.4 s, ~0.4 s after Dolby Vision engages); reported, the
+ * compositor removed the output and added it back (windows recreated, the
+ * saved configuration applied again). Until linux-yblod 7.3-7 KWin held the
+ * output 3 s itself (kwin-big-fella-hotplug-hold.patch); i915 has
+ * i915.hpd_hold_ms. A real unplug is reported after the delay.
+ */
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(hdmi_hpd_debounce_delay_ms, "HDMI HPD disconnect debounce delay in milliseconds (0 to disable, 1500 is common; big-fella: 3000 by default)");
 module_param_named(hdmi_hpd_debounce_delay_ms, amdgpu_hdmi_hpd_debounce_delay_ms, uint, 0644);
 
 /**
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_ddi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_ddi.c
index 02a53c9848e1..7cd3b5dad423 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_ddi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_ddi.c
@@ -4842,6 +4842,27 @@ static int intel_hdmi_reset_link(struct intel_encoder *encoder,
 	 * would be perfectly happy if were to just reconfigure
 	 * the SCDC settings on the fly.
 	 */
+	/*
+	 * big-fella: at most 3 of these in 20 s, in case the sink drops HPD
+	 * and resets its SCDC again after each (intel_ddi_hotplug looks again
+	 * after every hotplug): a link left wrong beats a screen that blanks
+	 * for ever.
+	 */
+	if (!connector->hdmi_scdc_fixes ||
+	    time_after(jiffies, connector->hdmi_scdc_fix_since + 20 * HZ)) {
+		connector->hdmi_scdc_fixes = 0;
+		connector->hdmi_scdc_fix_since = jiffies;
+	}
+	if (connector->hdmi_scdc_fixes >= 3) {
+		drm_err(display->drm, "[CONNECTOR:%d:%s] Sink's TMDS config 0x%02x still wrong after 3 modesets, leaving it\n",
+			connector->base.base.id, connector->base.name, config);
+		return 0;
+	}
+	connector->hdmi_scdc_fixes++;
+	drm_info(display->drm, "[CONNECTOR:%d:%s] Sink's TMDS config 0x%02x doesn't match the link (scrambling %s, 1/%d), modeset\n",
+		 connector->base.base.id, connector->base.name, config,
+		 str_yes_no(crtc_state->hdmi_scrambling),
+		 crtc_state->hdmi_high_tmds_clock_ratio ? 40 : 10);
 	return intel_modeset_commit_pipes(display, BIT(crtc->pipe), ctx);
 }
 
@@ -4873,7 +4894,20 @@ intel_ddi_hotplug(struct intel_encoder *encoder,
 	state = intel_encoder_hotplug(encoder, connector);
 
 	if (!intel_tc_port_link_reset(dig_port)) {
-		if (connector->base.connector_type == DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_HDMIA) {
+		/*
+		 * big-fella: not while HPD is held low (intel_hdmi_detect,
+		 * i915.hpd_hold_ms): the sink isn't answering then, and its SCDC
+		 * read as 0x00 forced up to three modesets, 3.5-4 s of black after
+		 * every Dolby Vision stop on an LG G5. HPD coming back is a new
+		 * hotplug (hotplug_retries from 0), so linux-9913's recheck still
+		 * looks at the sink for 4 s from then.
+		 */
+		if (connector->base.connector_type == DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_HDMIA &&
+		    connector->hpd_held) {
+			drm_dbg_kms(encoder->base.dev,
+				    "[CONNECTOR:%d:%s] HPD held low, SCDC not checked\n",
+				    connector->base.base.id, connector->base.name);
+		} else if (connector->base.connector_type == DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_HDMIA) {
 			intel_modeset_lock_ctx_retry(&ctx, NULL, 0, ret)
 				ret = intel_hdmi_reset_link(encoder, &ctx);
 			drm_WARN_ON(encoder->base.dev, ret);
@@ -4909,6 +4943,32 @@ intel_ddi_hotplug(struct intel_encoder *encoder,
 	    !dig_port->dp.is_mst)
 		state = INTEL_HOTPLUG_RETRY;
 
+	/*
+	 * big-fella: a TV that drops HPD for a moment as it changes picture
+	 * mode (an LG G5 does, ~0.4 s after a Dolby Vision or refresh rate
+	 * change) can reset its SCDC TMDS_Config *after* intel_hdmi_reset_link
+	 * above read it as matching: it then expects a 1/10 TMDS bit clock
+	 * ratio while we send 1/40 at 594 MHz, a valid signal it shows as "No
+	 * signal" until the next modeset. Seen on petunia 2026-10-29
+	 * (TMDS_Config 0x01 against hdmi_high_tmds_clock_ratio). So after any
+	 * hotplug of a connected HDMI sink, look again once a second for 4 s,
+	 * also when the hotplug changed the connector's status (which the
+	 * retry above doesn't cover); intel_hdmi_reset_link does nothing
+	 * unless the link scrambles or runs at 1/40, and a full modeset only
+	 * if the sink's SCDC disagrees.
+	 */
+	connector->hdmi_scdc_recheck =
+		connector->base.connector_type == DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_HDMIA &&
+		connector->base.status == connector_status_connected &&
+		connector->hotplug_retries < 4;
+	if (state == INTEL_HOTPLUG_UNCHANGED && connector->hdmi_scdc_recheck)
+		state = INTEL_HOTPLUG_RETRY;
+
+	/* big-fella: HPD held low (intel_hdmi_detect): look again until it's
+	 * back or the hold is up */
+	if (state == INTEL_HOTPLUG_UNCHANGED && connector->hpd_held)
+		state = INTEL_HOTPLUG_RETRY;
+
 	return state;
 }
 
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_display_types.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_display_types.h
index fcb71fb2bd46..cecbee83d6e4 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_display_types.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_display_types.h
@@ -556,6 +556,15 @@ struct intel_connector {
 
 	/* Number of times hotplug detection was tried after an HPD interrupt */
 	int hotplug_retries;
+	/* big-fella: look at an HDMI sink's SCDC again after this hotplug (intel_ddi_hotplug) */
+	bool hdmi_scdc_recheck;
+	/* big-fella: modesets intel_hdmi_reset_link made since hdmi_scdc_fix_since (at most 3 in 20 s) */
+	int hdmi_scdc_fixes;
+	unsigned long hdmi_scdc_fix_since;
+	/* big-fella: HPD low on a connected HDMI sink with a CRTC, reported as
+	 * connected since hpd_low_since (intel_hdmi_detect, i915.hpd_hold_ms) */
+	bool hpd_held;
+	unsigned long hpd_low_since;
 
 	/* since POLL and HPD connectors may use the same HPD line keep the native
 	   state of connector->polled in case hotplug storm detection changes it */
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_hdmi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_hdmi.c
index 6fa994869fa2..b57ae8023f91 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_hdmi.c
@@ -3215,6 +3215,50 @@ intel_hdmi_set_edid(struct drm_connector *_connector)
 	return connected;
 }
 
+/*
+ * big-fella: TVs drop HPD for a moment when they change picture mode (an LG
+ * G5 for ~0.4 s, ~0.4 s after Dolby Vision engages). Reported as is, the
+ * compositor removes the output and adds it again: windows recreated, the
+ * saved configuration applied again, a blank. While a connected HDMI sink has
+ * a CRTC, HPD low is reported as still connected (the EDID kept) for up to
+ * hpd_hold_ms; intel_ddi_hotplug looks again every second meanwhile, so a real
+ * unplug is reported once the time is up. Until linux-yblod 7.3-7 KWin did
+ * this itself (kwin-big-fella-hotplug-hold.patch, 3 s). 0 turns it off.
+ */
+static unsigned int hpd_hold_ms = 3000;
+module_param(hpd_hold_ms, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(hpd_hold_ms,
+	"HDMI: ms an HPD drop of a sink with an active output is reported as still "
+	"connected (big-fella; default 3000, 0 off)");
+
+static bool intel_hdmi_hpd_hold(struct intel_connector *connector)
+{
+	struct intel_display *display = to_intel_display(connector);
+
+	if (!hpd_hold_ms || connector->base.status != connector_status_connected ||
+	    !connector->base.state || !connector->base.state->crtc) {
+		connector->hpd_held = false;
+		return false;
+	}
+
+	if (!connector->hpd_held) {
+		connector->hpd_held = true;
+		connector->hpd_low_since = jiffies;
+		drm_info(display->drm, "[CONNECTOR:%d:%s] HPD low with an active output, still connected for up to %u ms\n",
+			 connector->base.base.id, connector->base.name, hpd_hold_ms);
+		return true;
+	}
+
+	if (time_before(jiffies, connector->hpd_low_since + msecs_to_jiffies(hpd_hold_ms)))
+		return true;
+
+	connector->hpd_held = false;
+	drm_info(display->drm, "[CONNECTOR:%d:%s] HPD still low after %u ms, disconnected\n",
+		 connector->base.base.id, connector->base.name,
+		 jiffies_to_msecs(jiffies - connector->hpd_low_since));
+	return false;
+}
+
 static enum drm_connector_status
 intel_hdmi_detect(struct drm_connector *_connector, bool force)
 {
@@ -3237,8 +3281,18 @@ intel_hdmi_detect(struct drm_connector *_connector, bool force)
 	wakeref = intel_display_power_get(display, POWER_DOMAIN_GMBUS);
 
 	if (DISPLAY_VER(display) >= 11 &&
-	    !intel_digital_port_connected(encoder))
+	    !intel_digital_port_connected(encoder)) {
+		/* big-fella: a short HPD drop isn't an unplug (hpd_hold_ms) */
+		if (intel_hdmi_hpd_hold(connector))
+			status = connector_status_connected;
 		goto out;
+	}
+
+	if (connector->hpd_held)
+		drm_info(display->drm, "[CONNECTOR:%d:%s] HPD back after %u ms\n",
+			 connector->base.base.id, connector->base.name,
+			 jiffies_to_msecs(jiffies - connector->hpd_low_since));
+	connector->hpd_held = false;
 
 	intel_hdmi_unset_edid(&connector->base);
 
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_hotplug.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_hotplug.c
index 970aa95ee344..267fc6b122cc 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_hotplug.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_hotplug.c
@@ -472,7 +472,7 @@ static void i915_hotplug_work_func(struct work_struct *work)
 	struct intel_hotplug *hotplug = &display->hotplug;
 	struct drm_connector_list_iter conn_iter;
 	struct intel_connector *connector;
-	u32 changed = 0, retry = 0;
+	u32 changed = 0, retry = 0, recheck = 0;
 	u32 hpd_event_bits;
 	u32 hpd_retry_bits;
 	struct drm_connector *first_changed_connector = NULL;
@@ -536,6 +536,9 @@ static void i915_hotplug_work_func(struct work_struct *work)
 					drm_connector_get(&connector->base);
 					first_changed_connector = &connector->base;
 				}
+				/* big-fella: and look again (intel_ddi_hotplug) */
+				if (connector->hdmi_scdc_recheck)
+					recheck |= hpd_bit;
 				break;
 			case INTEL_HOTPLUG_RETRY:
 				retry |= hpd_bit;
@@ -556,6 +559,8 @@ static void i915_hotplug_work_func(struct work_struct *work)
 
 	/* Remove shared HPD pins that have changed */
 	retry &= ~changed;
+	/* big-fella: but not an HDMI sink's SCDC recheck (intel_ddi_hotplug) */
+	retry |= recheck;
 	if (retry) {
 		spin_lock_irq(&display->irq.lock);
 		display->hotplug.retry_bits |= retry;
